@page "/about"
@model AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = SiteText.NavAbout;
    var site = SiteText.SiteName;
}
@functions {
    // The contact as text, or linked when Site:ContactUrl is set.
    private Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html.IHtmlContent ContactHtml() =>
        Model.ContactUrl is null
            ? new Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html.HtmlString(SiteHtml.Encode(Model.Contact))
            : new Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html.HtmlString($"<a href=\"{SiteHtml.Encode(Model.ContactUrl)}\">{SiteHtml.Encode(Model.Contact)}</a>");
}
<article class="prose">
    <h1>About @site</h1>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>@site is an unofficial website for looking up IUCN Red List assessments and citing them on English Wikipedia. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by IUCN. It is free and has no ads.</p>
    <p>Each taxon on the IUCN Red List has a page with:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>the category, criteria and population trend of its latest global assessment, with the date assessed and the year published</li>
        <li>its earlier global assessments, and its latest assessment in each region</li>
        <li>common names and synonyms, and for a species, the subspecies and varieties that IUCN, the Catalogue of Life and Wikidata list</li>
        <li>its status in other conservation lists that include it: the CITES appendices, Australia's EPBC Act and state and territory lists (as SPRAT records them), Brazil's national assessments of its fauna (ICMBio), the UK's red lists, wildlife laws and priority species lists (as JNCC records them), the US Endangered Species Act, Canada's COSEWIC and Species at Risk Act, NatureServe's global, national and state, province and territory ranks, and the New Zealand Threat Classification System</li>
        <li>links to the assessment on the IUCN Red List website, the English Wikipedia article, the Wikidata item and the Catalogue of Life page, and for Australian species the SPRAT profile</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each taxon also has a wikitext page, linked from the Tools menu at the top of its page and the Tools section at the bottom. For any of the taxon's assessments, it has:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>wikitext to copy into Wikipedia: a {{cite iucn}} citation, an {{IUCN status}} template, and the taxobox status parameters (status, status_system and status_ref), labelled with the taxobox the article most likely uses: {{Speciesbox}} for a species, {{Subspeciesbox}} for an animal subspecies, and {{Infraspeciesbox}} for a plant or fungus subspecies or a variety</li>
        <li>a {{cite Q}} citation of the assessment's Wikidata item, or QuickStatements commands to create that item</li>
        <li>for the latest global assessment of a species or subspecies, QuickStatements commands that bring the IUCN conservation status on its Wikidata item up to date</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Some taxa with no current assessment also have pages: old IUCN ids of taxa that now have another id, and taxa that IUCN no longer assesses. These pages show the taxon's earlier assessments, and their wikitext pages give wikitext for each.</p>
    <p>The <a href="/update">status update page</a> updates the IUCN statuses in pasted wikitext ({{IUCN status}} templates, status columns in wikitables, and taxoboxes) to match the latest global assessments. It does not save the text.</p>
    <p>Search matches scientific names, common names in any language, and synonyms.</p>

    <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>This site is run by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Pengo">User:Pengo</a>, an English Wikipedia editor who also runs the Wikipedia bot account <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Beastie_Bot">Beastie Bot</a>.</p>
    <p>To report a wrong citation, a wrong link or another problem with this site, contact @ContactHtml(). Include the address of the page.</p>
    <p>If a category or another detail is also wrong on the IUCN Red List website, the error is in IUCN's data. Report it to IUCN through the IUCN Red List website.</p>
    <p>The source code of this site, and of the tools that build its database, is on GitHub: <a href="@SiteText.SourceCodeUrl">pengowray/BeastieBot3</a>.</p>
    <p>The bat logo is by spiky.fish.</p>

    <h2>Logs and privacy</h2>
    <p>The server keeps a log of each request for 14 days: the time, the address of the page (which includes any search text), the IP address and the browser's user agent. The log is used to see how the site is used and to stop abuse. Text pasted into the status update page is not logged or saved.</p>
    <p>The site sets no cookies and uses no analytics. The theme you choose is kept in your browser.</p>

    <h2>Data sources</h2>
    <p>This site reformats and combines the data from these sources.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
